the lords of the clans  within the samurai could use for their  clans by adopting them into the family  if they wanted to kind of like how shima  are playing to do with jin later in the  game  rizu had personally invited some of the  lords to watch as he was a lonely  fighter and was fighting the heir to the  clan sakai  jin and this was his opportunity to  prove himself specific actions and  events though would cause this to not be  successful for reuse though this was  jin's first tournament so he was very  thrilled to fight and went all out right  from the start  which gave ryuzo a lousy look as he lost  fairly quickly  on top of this defeat the clans were  more interested in what the future of  clan sakai had as opposed to some  no-name fighter not only because jin was  part of a clan within the island already  which gave him more status than ryuzo  but mostly due in part that jin was  already going to be a samurai and if by  some reason the island got into a civil  war  the clans need to know the strength of  the other rival clans even though they  stuck together during the invasion it's  not uncommon for a clan to feel  indifferent about its position compared  to others  maybe they have the worst terrain on the  island or always hit the hardest  politically it only takes one person to  start a war so this tournament to some  could be used as a gathering of intel  regardless though ryuzo was not happy  with this outcome and still continually  brings it up to jhin even now  because this re-user needs to find  mercenary rick to try to prove himself  and to others that he was capable of  being a samurai so he joined the straw  hats and later became the leader fast  forward back to the present day  ryuzo and jin are having a little  reunion after their encounter with some  mongol forces to discuss their plans  at this moment as explained before jin  is looking for allies to save lord  shimra  the problem is that ryuzo needs help  their numbers are shrinking and those  few members they have left  are starving so jin proposes a plan if  they find enough food to survive the  straw hats will then help jin save  shimra as a sign of thanks  riza was hesitant as his men are all he  has but ends up agreeing but only on the  terms they find the food first you then  arrive at the straw hat encampment to  discuss the plans on how to get the  group the food they need  it's discovered here that the straw hats  were at komoda beach but the only reason  they lived  is that they ran away when it got rough  while this is a small detail it reveals  that ryuza doesn't really carry the same  codes of virtue that jin follows being a  samurai  as leader reuses men are his top  priority no matter the cost  the small instances we see of this in  the beginning is the game's way of  foreshadowing what lies ahead  jin then arrives at taku-sudama cemetery  where he meets ryuzo to discuss the  intel his straw heads have discovered  about the nearby base  the plan is to infiltrate the lighthouse  on the nearby hill to prevent  reinforcements from coming off shore  upon clearing the lighthouse it is found  that the dock they are near  is only for transport the food is being  stationed there so they can ship it  offshore  so the straw hats distract the mongols  while jin and reuse those sneak onto the  ship to find the food they were shipping  once again ryuza comes back empty-handed  is after searching all the boats in the  bay  none had any food all isn't lost though  as the document with mongol battle plans  is found which could lead to some of the  supply lines containing some food later  then jin eventually goes to kamatsu  forge and takes it from mongol control  out of the blue ryuzo shows up and asks  chin for help rizzo's men use the battle  plans they seized from the previous  encounter and got outnumbered and  captured  but strangely enough the straw hats were  singing people who are captors don't  usually sing while in captivity you  follow ryuza and the rest of the straw  hats who weren't captured to for yatate  the plans to sneak in  rescue the straw hats then ambush  mongols when everyone is free this is a  relatively simple task as now with the  straw hats being reunited you overwhelm  the mongols with ease after talking with  ryuza the reason for their singing  within captivity is due to them being  fed food as we stated before the straw  hats are surviving so a feast of some  excellent food is worthy of a  celebration  with everything all set and ready though  jin with his new allies take the forward  to castle canada  except there's just one problem upon  arriving everyone has shown up  except the straw hats the problem is  that there's no time to wait so the  attack continues without their support  the reason they aren't at the front  gates with jinn is that they've already  infiltrated the castle themselves  except for the wrong reason the khan has  placed a bounty on jyn's head  and anyone can claim it ryuzo accepted  the offer but he still needs food for  his men  jin tries to convince him to have him  join his side once more but ryuzo knows  that even if he does and becomes the  samurai  he'd be leaving his men defend for  themselves and probably just get sent to  his death like a komoda beach and ryuza  does not want that to happen  so joining the khan is his only viable  option gina ryuzo duel within the walls  of the castle  jin then defeats ryuza but leaves him  alive and wounded  jin gives him one final chance to  surrender and join his side  but ryuza declines once more alerting  the castle of jin's position and  escaping to the gate  this is the very last chance ryozo had  but still chose to stick with his  previous decision  there's no more going back on this as  jyn and ryuzo are no longer friends and  the next time they meet  one is leaving alive the rest of this  encounter is played out normally with  jin rescuing lord shimra and securing  the castle we get a glimpse of what  ryuzo is now dealing with as a result of  his decision which is attacking villages  and forts with the khan and killing  people as a way to get them to surrender  riza seems displeased with his actions  he has taken but he knows not only can  he not go back on his word now  he also understands that he and his men  need to survive and proving his worth to  the khan is the only way to do so after  capturing the castle ryuzo takes a back  seat in terms of some screen time but  there is one dialogue that is shown  between ryuzo and kotun khan which talks  about the khan's order to kill jin  rizo initially refuses but khan  pressures him into accepting  reason that comes up with a plan that  involves him not being killed  this leads us to the end of act 2 right  before the assault on castle shimra  jin receives a word from schumer that  the straw hats plan to flank the samurai  when they attack and that jin needs to  deal with this  issue before they can proceed with the  assault jin then enters the stronghold  to find ryuza they talk for a bit before  jin is knocked out unconscious and taken  captive along with taka who joined jin  in an attempt to prove himself that he  isn't just a liability and he can hold  his own this capture of course leads to  taka's death and jin's ruthless  emotion-filled slaughter of the rest of  the camp's occupants  the conclusion of this story though  comes at the end of the raid of the  castle  jyn after poisoning the guards the  castle walks up to the stairs to the  main building  and hopes to find kotoon khan but  instead finds ryuzo in his place  this then starts the final encounter  with ryuzo that jin will have rizzo  tells jin  that he doesn't want to fight this time  very opposite rules compared to the last  fight they had  jyn doesn't accept as ryuza was an  accomplice in taka's death  rizzo comes up with ideas to make it  believable that he wasn't a traitor but  jin won't budge  rizzo is a criminal and he must pay for  his crimes with this comes the last  battle between the two with ryuza being  killed as a result this ends the tale  between ryuzo  and jin it's a sad tale though rizzo  being a jin side would have been really  incredible especially at the ending of  the game  but of course the two of them had  different priorities which led him down  this path that would ultimately be his  last let me know what you think about  this encounter though between these two  in the comments down below  as always i want to thank you all for  joining me on this journey of two old  friends doing all they can to survive  of course but with different ideals that  force them to cross paths and confront  one another so that the victor may  continue to survive and do what they  think is right thank you for watching  the video though like and subscribe if  you enjoyed these narrative commentaries  and i'll hopefully see you all in a  future video  [Music]  goodbye  [Music]  you
 

